<h2>How well does Pi handle MCP servers compared to GitHub plugins?</h2>
<p class="answer">Pi handles standard MCP servers via <code>pi mcp list</code> at roughly the same rate as Codex and Cursor, while plugins installed as GitHub Pi packages depend on whether the repository follows Pi's skill directory layout.</p>
[[SMX:PI_MCP_VS_PLUGIN_HTML]]
<p>In our Nov 20, 2026 baseline (<code>testing/results/2026-11-20.json</code>), Pi passed 9 of 9 reference MCP servers (100%) and 21 of 45 npm MCP servers (46.7%), right in line with Codex (8/9 and 22/45) and Cursor (9/9 and 23/45). By contrast, Pi passed 55 of 86 plugins (64.0%) because several repos only expose Claude Code plugin layouts without Pi-compatible skill paths. Browse verified Pi-ready add-ons at <a href="/works-in/pi/">what works in Pi</a>.</p>

